{
	chapter.0750595BB1E99F0F.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 2. The subways. Something lives down there."]
	chapter.0750595BB1E99F0F.title: "Below the Line"
	chapter.08818A63B866F9C2.chapter_subtitle: ["MineColonies, one step at a time. Citizens do the work."]
	chapter.08818A63B866F9C2.title: "Your Colony"
	chapter.1974464A24A05158.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 4. Where the Builders fled, and when you are ready to follow."]
	chapter.1974464A24A05158.title: "Other Doors"
	chapter.1E78474C245FD8CA.chapter_subtitle: ["Create, one machine at a time. Trains and airships at the end."]
	chapter.1E78474C245FD8CA.title: "The Builders' Craft"
	chapter.25B77CDE329F5438.chapter_subtitle: ["How the fungus grows, and how to turn its body against it."]
	chapter.25B77CDE329F5438.title: "The Infection"
	chapter.2FDC441E816C66D8.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 5. Airships, rockets, and the end of the line."]
	chapter.2FDC441E816C66D8.title: "Above"
	chapter.4DB226BD3A09B8E8.chapter_subtitle: ["The last train dropped you here. It left without you."]
	chapter.4DB226BD3A09B8E8.title: "Arrival"
	chapter.4DB557D8844B1D84.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 6. The end of the line."]
	chapter.4DB557D8844B1D84.title: "The Engine"
	chapter.5829F60643377E5B.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 3. The infection spreads. Hold the line."]
	chapter.5829F60643377E5B.title: "Lights Out"
	chapter.60BB903992A168B6.chapter_subtitle: ["Each one has rules. Learn them before they learn you."]
	chapter.60BB903992A168B6.title: "Know Your Horrors"
	chapter.7E45EDCAAD68086A.chapter_subtitle: ["Act 1. Make a home. Light a district."]
	chapter.7E45EDCAAD68086A.title: "The Platform"
	chapter_group.151E3065A6314194.title: "The Line"
	chapter_group.3095EA91149B5FEF.title: "Field Guides"
	quest.009EFC3604D9FFD1.quest_desc: ["Below the platforms: a cradle of iron and gears with nothing in it, and scorch marks where something was torn out in a hurry.", "", "The Builders pulled the Engine's &eheart&r to carry it away. They never got it out of the capital. You find it in a guard's locker, wrapped in a coat.", "", "Check this to take it. &7It is a beacon. It is warm.&r"]
	quest.009EFC3604D9FFD1.quest_subtitle: "It beats when I talk."
	quest.009EFC3604D9FFD1.title: "The Heart"
	quest.03622A4EF48DF367.quest_desc: ["Get off the ground: a Create Aeronautics airship (see &eThe Builders' Craft&r). Check this once you are flying over the city."]
	quest.03622A4EF48DF367.title: "Airborne"
	quest.03C973DA0DB6534E.quest_desc: ["Obsidian frame (needs a diamond pickaxe), light it. Bring back &eglowstone dust&r: you need it for the next door."]
	quest.03C973DA0DB6534E.title: "2. The Burning Below"
	quest.0408B65C8C597F09.quest_desc: ["Your first infected weapon: the &eCleaver&r (fleshy bone + fleshy claw + living core). Infected weapons hit infected hard."]
	quest.0408B65C8C597F09.title: "Fight Fire With Flesh"
	quest.06012264A7AEEF88.quest_desc: ["Fungus is spreading out of the deep places, turning everything it touches. This one you &ecan&r fight, and you should, early.", "", "Open &eThe Infection&r guide. It explains how it grows and how you turn its own body against it.", "", "&7Stencilled on a rusted valve wheel: &o\"BURN RATE LOW. IF IT SLOWS, THE FUEL GETS OUT.\"&r"]
	quest.06012264A7AEEF88.title: "It Spreads"
	quest.0710F468B9CB220E.quest_desc: ["&cThe Warden&r. Blind. Huge. It finds you by sound and smell, and it hits harder than anything else down here.", "", "The smart move is to never meet it. If you have to kill it, bring the whole crew, the best armor you own and a plan: it hits through shields, and from range it fires a &3sonic boom&r through walls.", "", "&cTip:&r it digs back into the ground if it can't find anyone for a minute. Hiding works."]
	quest.0710F468B9CB220E.quest_subtitle: "We were so quiet. It came anyway."
	quest.0710F468B9CB220E.title: "Don't Wake It"
	quest.071CBECFD52B939C.quest_desc: ["They move only when unseen. Keep eyes on them, back away, break them with a pickaxe. Never blink near one."]
	quest.071CBECFD52B939C.title: "Weeping Angels"
	quest.08794E63595E59BC.quest_desc: ["Walls, a door and a bed before the first night. Something may knock. &cDo not answer.&r"]
	quest.08794E63595E59BC.title: "Somewhere To Hide"
	quest.091946D95301C968.quest_desc: ["&cThe Pale Demon&r doesn't come at you itself. It &cwears&r things: cows, pigs, villagers, even golems. A possessed animal watches you, doesn't eat, and follows.", "", "&eThe rules:&r crosses keep it off (a &eWooden Cross&r is sticks with redstone in the crossbar), and &eHoly Water&r hurts it. It likes old mines, ruined churches and anywhere people used to be.", "", "&cTip:&r never sleep near livestock you didn't raise yourself. Get the cross to check this."]
	quest.091946D95301C968.quest_subtitle: "The cow was looking at me. Cows don't do that."
	quest.091946D95301C968.title: "The Pale Demon"
	quest.0B9F12FC3A0D76DB.quest_desc: ["In a Builder office at the edge of the city, a logbook:", "&o\"Day 41. The things from below follow the dark. The growth down here listens: we went quiet and it let us pass. We're moving everyone out by rail. The Engine at the end of the line holds them back as long as it turns.\"&r", "", "The last entry is one word, over and over: &cLIGHTS&r.", "", "Check this once you have read it. The infection is waking up top."]
	quest.0B9F12FC3A0D76DB.quest_subtitle: "Day 41. Their handwriting gets worse after this."
	quest.0B9F12FC3A0D76DB.title: "The Evacuation Log"
	quest.0BB47AB5BB349F1C.quest_desc: ["When the Builder's Hut is done, right-click the &eTown Hall&r block and press &eBuild&r. The builder works on one thing at a time."]
	quest.0BB47AB5BB349F1C.title: "Build the Town Hall"
	quest.0BD78C385D754CE9.quest_desc: ["Armor plates (fragment + fiber + nerves) make &eplated armor&r. Later it grafts with flesh armor into Living armor."]
	quest.0BD78C385D754CE9.title: "Plated"
	quest.0BF299613535445C.quest_desc: ["Statues that only move when nobody looks. &cDo not charge these.&r Keep eyes on them and break them with a pickaxe."]
	quest.0BF299613535445C.title: "Don't Blink"
	quest.0C8CE3E83291AEEB.quest_desc: ["Place the &eSupply Camp&r, open its chest, place the &eTown Hall&r block. Right-click it and create your colony.", "", "Placing any hut only puts down one block. The building itself comes later, from your builder."]
	quest.0C8CE3E83291AEEB.title: "Town Hall"
	quest.0D0ADCDCEBD811C1.quest_desc: ["Someone at the edge of your vision. Standing still. Gone when you look again.", "", "The &eKnow Your Horrors&r guide has the rules for each of them."]
	quest.0D0ADCDCEBD811C1.title: "Being Watched"
	quest.0E6E06DCBF855D4D.quest_desc: ["Compound plate + a &eredstone block&r + redstone. The base of every Cryo piece."]
	quest.0E6E06DCBF855D4D.title: "Reinforced Plate"
	quest.11980281AE97CA15.quest_desc: ["Now and then, when you are deep in the ruined city at night or underground, a &eradio call&r crackles in: someone barricaded in the dark. It is marked on your map.", "", "Break through the fences, deal with what waits at the door, and &ebring them home&r. They join your crew if there is room, or stay as a guest. If nobody comes, the signal goes quiet. It will not come often."]
	quest.11980281AE97CA15.title: "Voices in the Ruins"
	quest.12D403627C0AEF51.quest_desc: ["A Builder note, scratched into a wall: &o\"They don't come where the lights are on. KEEP IT LIT.\"&r", "", "Light up your colony. Lanterns, torches, anything."]
	quest.12D403627C0AEF51.title: "Keep It Lit"
	quest.1300434F59C13300.quest_desc: ["Casing, a seat, controls and a bogey on the rails make a train. Assemble it at the station."]
	quest.1300434F59C13300.title: "Driver's Seat"
	quest.1305B2D2B4C15A61.quest_desc: ["The infection only grows where players are, but it grows fast. Do these early:", "1. A &eGas Mask&r.", "2. &bCryo-Combat boots&r: they clear spore plants as you walk.", "3. &bIce bombs&r to push it back.", "4. A &bC.D.U.&r at the edge of the colony.", "&cNever let infected get kills&r: every kill makes them evolve."]
	quest.1305B2D2B4C15A61.title: "Before It's Too Late"
	quest.132F17720563244A.quest_desc: ["Deep in the Deep Dark there is an &eAncient City&r: stone halls, soul fire, and an empty frame in the middle like a station gate with no train.", "", "The Builders found it first. Their notes call it &o\"the first station\"&r: the city under the city. Somebody built a line out of here a long time before they did.", "", "Find one and walk into it. They are rare: a few thousand blocks apart.", "", "&cTip:&r the frame in the centre is a door. It needs a heart to open."]
	quest.132F17720563244A.quest_subtitle: "Someone built this before the Builders did."
	quest.132F17720563244A.title: "The First Station"
	quest.1371453DC1ED0B74.quest_desc: ["A press over a depot flattens ingots into &esheets&r. Iron sheets go into almost every machine."]
	quest.1371453DC1ED0B74.title: "The Press"
	quest.137D6F7597708837.quest_desc: ["Get a &eBuilder's Hut&r. With it in your inventory, right-click the ground with the &eBuild Tool&r, pick it, place it, then right-click the hut block and press &eBuild&r. Your builder builds their own hut first."]
	quest.137D6F7597708837.title: "Hire a Builder"
	quest.13EDA76AF227D376.quest_desc: ["From the sky you can finally see it: the capital, and the &eEngine&r at the end of every rail line, barely turning.", "", "The rails all run in. None run out. &eThe Engine&r is next."]
	quest.13EDA76AF227D376.quest_subtitle: "Chapter Gate"
	quest.13EDA76AF227D376.title: "The End of the Line"
	quest.16BCAEAEADC90F46.quest_desc: ["A &eTentacle Rig&r carries you over floors, walls and ceilings. It runs on a &ecopper backtank's&r air.", "", "Build it on &emechanical crafters&r: &f4&r tentacles, a precision mechanism, &f2&r brass casings, a copper sheet and a copper backtank in the middle.", "", "&cTip:&r refill it under a spinning shaft like any backtank. Crafting it does &cnot&r keep the old tank's air.", "", "Over a chasm, nothing in these tunnels can reach you on a ceiling."]
	quest.16BCAEAEADC90F46.quest_subtitle: "Down here, the ceiling is the safest floor."
	quest.16BCAEAEADC90F46.title: "Eight Hands"
	quest.17417239150B9BF0.quest_desc: ["Track is made in a press, or pried out of the subways (much faster)."]
	quest.17417239150B9BF0.title: "Lay Track"
	quest.18B606392431482E.quest_desc: ["The moon goes red and everything comes at once. Survive a &cBlood Moon&r together, then check this. Your colony is what they come for."]
	quest.18B606392431482E.title: "Blood Moon"
	quest.1AB47B6183704461.quest_desc: ["The one you fight. See &eThe Infection&r guide."]
	quest.1AB47B6183704461.title: "The Infection"
	quest.1D9E3D56B93511C0.quest_desc: ["It creeps up while you're not looking. Keep checking behind you, and stick with your group."]
	quest.1D9E3D56B93511C0.title: "The Obsessed"
	quest.1E20243C628D2135.quest_desc: ["A &erecovery compass&r is a compass ringed with &f8&r echo shards. It points to the spot where you last died.", "", "Down here that is worth more than a sword. keepInventory saves your gear, but your &elights, track and markers&r are still out there, and so is the way back.", "", "&cTip:&r it spins if you haven't died in this world. Hope it spins."]
	quest.1E20243C628D2135.quest_subtitle: "It points at the last place I gave up."
	quest.1E20243C628D2135.title: "Back to Where You Fell"
	quest.1E34D759428F025C.quest_desc: ["Something huge coils in the courtyard ruins. The first Twilight boss."]
	quest.1E34D759428F025C.title: "The Serpent"
	quest.1EA0D0D0D0CCD83B.quest_desc: ["A builder out of materials shows a speech bubble. Right-click the &eBuilder's Hut&r block to see the list, and put the items in its storage. They fetch them from there."]
	quest.1EA0D0D0D0CCD83B.title: "What They Need"
	quest.1F0641D17582BAE9.quest_desc: ["A red, infected-player boss that turns up near Protos and in the last ordeal. It drops a lot of reforged biomass of all three kinds."]
	quest.1F0641D17582BAE9.title: "The FIXER"
	quest.201CFB685EC22A4C.quest_desc: ["Hold the &eBuilder's Hut&r, right-click the ground with the &eBuild Tool&r, pick it, move the preview, confirm. Right-click the hut block and press &eBuild&r. A citizen becomes your builder and builds this hut first."]
	quest.201CFB685EC22A4C.title: "Your Builder"
	quest.20BC1DE9290ABEE6.quest_desc: ["A schedule runs a train with no driver, like the ghost trains still circling the city."]
	quest.20BC1DE9290ABEE6.title: "On Schedule"
	quest.20FED50174954243.quest_desc: ["A &cProto Hivemind&r runs the outbreak around it. Kill it and that infection loses its mind. Go together, fully geared."]
	quest.20FED50174954243.title: "Something Once Great"
	quest.21BF5EF159226398.quest_desc: ["Citizens need a &eResidence&r. Place one with the Build Tool and press Build on it. More homes, more citizens."]
	quest.21BF5EF159226398.title: "A Roof for Everyone"
	quest.2227FE9F824CE158.quest_desc: ["Copper + zinc in a heated mixer. Brass is the jump from simple machines to trains."]
	quest.2227FE9F824CE158.title: "Brass"
	quest.224F2A5123C5E4F8.quest_desc: ["Your crew are people, not tools. Stand near one who is not busy and just &etalk&r: &o\"how are you?\"&r", "", "The more they trust you (feed them, light their nights, stay close when they are scared), the more they open up: a memory of the Fall, a small favour, something they can teach, and in the end a change that stays. If one asks you to fetch something, the spot is marked on your map."]
	quest.224F2A5123C5E4F8.title: "Someone's Story"
	quest.22752B4DD6E870A5.quest_desc: ["Find one of the corrupted records in infected ruins. Somebody saw this coming."]
	quest.22752B4DD6E870A5.title: "Fragments of the Past"
	quest.253B69673D87FB1D.quest_desc: ["They got this far. Then the logs stop."]
	quest.253B69673D87FB1D.title: "Mars"
	quest.2572FA76C9A64D4E.quest_desc: ["An empty Builder outpost. Signs of a hasty departure. A logbook pointing further out.", "", "One line in it is underlined twice: &o\"Nobody stayed to turn it.\"&r"]
	quest.2572FA76C9A64D4E.title: "The Moon"
	quest.25D38220222EB9F7.quest_desc: ["First &eprepared water&r: a &egold nugget&r over &enether wart&r over a &eglass bottle&r. Then smelt it in a furnace into &eHoly Water&r.", "", "It is the strongest thing you have against the possessed.", "", "&cTip:&r nether wart only grows in the Nether (Act 4). Come back to this one later, and keep a bottle in your hotbar from then on."]
	quest.25D38220222EB9F7.quest_subtitle: "Gold, wart, fire. Somebody worked this out the hard way."
	quest.25D38220222EB9F7.title: "Holy Water"
	quest.26AFBD76102107E5.quest_desc: ["It turns. Near any rail you can hear it now: a low hum, like a train that never quite arrives.", "", "&eThey don't come where the lights are on.&r The Builders wrote it on every wall. Now it is true. No horror walks into the light, none comes near the Engine, and the dark gets out of the way of a train.", "", "The fungus still climbs toward the capital. It always will. Keep the line running. Keep it lit.", "", "&7The End of the Line.&r"]
	quest.26AFBD76102107E5.title: "The Line Holds"
	quest.2728033B3A3B1410.quest_desc: ["The tunnels are full of &eCreate track&r, and track is worth more than gold up top.", "", "Break it with a pickaxe and it drops as an item. Grab &f16&r: enough to lay your first line later in &eThe Builders' Craft&r.", "", "&cTip:&r don't strip the track you came in on. You will want it to find your way back, and so will the ghost trains.", "", "Next: somewhere down here the lamps still work. Find out how."]
	quest.2728033B3A3B1410.quest_subtitle: "Finders keepers. The owners aren't coming back."
	quest.2728033B3A3B1410.title: "Scavenge the Depot"
	quest.27684B7B1DD726AE.quest_desc: ["The Engine needs &efour minutes&r of turning to wake. Keep a cog spinning and stay near the heart. Everything infected for a mile will come to stop it.", "", "Take shifts on the crank. Cover whoever is turning. If the cogs stop, the count stops. If everyone leaves, it winds down. If you break it, you start again."]
	quest.27684B7B1DD726AE.title: "Keep It Turning"
	quest.2881FE965D56CE0A.quest_desc: ["Below the last subway line the rock turns black and the walls start to &3glow&r. This is the &3Deep Dark&r: the bottom of the world, around &fy -50&r.", "", "Walk into it and check this off. You won't see much. You aren't meant to.", "", "&cTip:&r &3sculk shriekers&r (the ones with bone jaws) call for something when they hear you. Break them from a distance, or don't touch them at all.", "", "Next: there is a city down here, older than the one up top."]
	quest.2881FE965D56CE0A.quest_subtitle: "It got quiet. Not the good kind."
	quest.2881FE965D56CE0A.title: "The Lowest Platform"
	quest.296B3A2F9AA64A1C.quest_desc: ["The &eWooden Cross&r is the Builders' version: &esticks&r, with &eredstone&r set in the middle of the crossbar (stick, redstone, stick on top; two sticks down).", "", "When something possessed gets close, this is what you hold up. A possessed animal looks normal until it doesn't: it watches you, it doesn't eat, it follows.", "", "&cTip:&r never sleep near livestock you didn't raise yourself.", "", "Next: the iron cross and holy water, if you can find the parts."]
	quest.296B3A2F9AA64A1C.quest_subtitle: "Red dust in the middle. Like a heartbeat."
	quest.296B3A2F9AA64A1C.title: "Something to Hold"
	quest.2AF367471295A5FB.quest_desc: ["&eSneak&r and use a &ewrench&r on the heart. Someone does the same within 15 seconds to confirm.", "", "The Engine stops for good. The fungus sinks back into the deep and starves. Nothing holds the dark any more.", "", "&7Only one of these two will ever be checked. It is one choice, for everyone on the server.&r"]
	quest.2AF367471295A5FB.title: "Let It Rest"
	quest.2B743B01E796CAA4.quest_desc: ["Pinned inside the locker door, in a careful hand:", "&o\"ENGINE, FIELD ASSEMBLY. Iron bed, three by three. Heart on the bed. A cog on each side of the heart, a casing in each corner. Track in sight. Then turn it.\"&r", "", "In plain words: &e9 iron blocks&r in a 3x3, the &ebeacon&r on the middle one, a &ecogwheel&r on each of its four sides and any &eCreate casing&r in the four corners (all level with the beacon), &etrack&r within 8 blocks, and something turning a cog: a &ehand crank&r on top of one is enough.", "", "Leave the sky above it open if you want to see it shine."]
	quest.2B743B01E796CAA4.title: "The Blueprint"
	quest.2CE34496659452AF.quest_desc: ["Big cannons on a mount. On an airship they recoil for real."]
	quest.2CE34496659452AF.title: "Broadside"
	quest.2CF20EADF8DBB3B0.quest_desc: ["One of each kind of &eReforged Biomass&r. This is what the strongest weapons are made from."]
	quest.2CF20EADF8DBB3B0.title: "Reforged"
	quest.2D07C5846DE20D19.quest_desc: ["Whatever hunts out here goes for whoever walks alone. Travel in pairs after dark."]
	quest.2D07C5846DE20D19.title: "Stay Together"
	quest.2F112779CCC1397F.quest_desc: ["Dispenser + compound plate + iron trapdoor + iron. Put the &bC.D.U.&r between the infection and your colony. Your crew can &eguard&r it too (\"everyone, guard the east side\")."]
	quest.2F112779CCC1397F.title: "Hold the Border"
	quest.31D27DBA25D73C48.quest_desc: ["A water wheel in flowing water spins forever. Your first power source. Hook a shaft to it."]
	quest.31D27DBA25D73C48.title: "Free Power"
	quest.32E2D7B5160D5AA5.quest_desc: ["They drop body parts: &emutated fiber&r, claw fragments, hearts. Keep everything. It is your crafting material from here on."]
	quest.32E2D7B5160D5AA5.title: "Harvest"
	quest.3450C0960C7F9112.quest_desc: ["Every way out you found, the Builders found first. None of them were far enough.", "", "The rails to the capital were cut. The only way left is &eup&r."]
	quest.3450C0960C7F9112.quest_subtitle: "Chapter Gate"
	quest.3450C0960C7F9112.title: "Every Door Leads Back"
	quest.34A77DF2BB0A6AAC.quest_desc: ["Protos send raids as the world's corruption rises: Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, each once. On this server they come later than normal. Keep the border frozen and they come later still."]
	quest.34A77DF2BB0A6AAC.title: "The Ordeals"
	quest.3528E3F6A212D15C.quest_desc: ["Tunnels and caves. It stalks, then runs. Light the way, don't go down alone."]
	quest.3528E3F6A212D15C.title: "The Cave Dweller"
	quest.353080D1B6B05A49.quest_desc: ["The capital is the oldest of the Lost Cities, and the farthest. Fly the way every rail line points: away from home, past the last line you rode, until the towers get taller and darker and the track runs into a wall and &cstops&r.", "", "That stub is the end of the line. If you cannot find one, make one: a rail that goes nowhere is enough. Mark it on the map for everyone (&e'&r), and check this when you are standing at it."]
	quest.353080D1B6B05A49.title: "The Capital"
	quest.37521462F21C1396.quest_desc: ["The Builders' last project. Read the &eAstrodux&r (Ad Astra's own guidebook) for the steps: steel, a rocket, fuel, an oxygen loader and a space suit."]
	quest.37521462F21C1396.title: "Higher Still"
	quest.37E669B44AB7A238.quest_desc: ["Some of the stone down here is not stone. The &cSilencing Golem&r looks like the cave wall until you walk past it.", "", "It hunts quiet tunnels. Watch for a patch of wall that sits slightly wrong, or a block that is there one second and gone the next.", "", "Kill one. Fight it in the light, with a friend watching your back.", "", "&cTip:&r carry a stack of cobblestone. Walling it off buys time."]
	quest.37E669B44AB7A238.quest_subtitle: "That wall wasn't there on the way in."
	quest.37E669B44AB7A238.title: "Wrong Rock"
	quest.3982EBB723ECD32B.quest_desc: ["Your settlement made it through the dark.", "", "On a dead radio, a repeating message: &o\"...doors open beyond the forest, beyond the sky... the Engine is at the end of the line...\"&r"]
	quest.3982EBB723ECD32B.quest_subtitle: "Chapter Gate"
	quest.3982EBB723ECD32B.title: "We Hold"
	quest.39CA5A0461F170FE.quest_desc: ["A working mine, once: carts, lamps, a crew's camp. The crew is gone. Their dinner is still on the table.", "", "Find the &eMiners' Mine&r. They are rare (a couple of thousand blocks apart), so mark one on the map for everyone (&e'&r) when you find it.", "", "&cTip:&r count the beds. Then count the people you find. The Pale Demon likes to stay where people were."]
	quest.39CA5A0461F170FE.quest_subtitle: "Six bunks. Six plates. Nobody."
	quest.39CA5A0461F170FE.title: "The Miners' Mine"
	quest.3A3C79C53B1E41FC.quest_desc: ["&e/claude <question>&r answers questions about the pack in chat. &e/report <problem>&r goes straight to the developer."]
	quest.3A3C79C53B1E41FC.title: "Ask the Pack"
	quest.3A6CCC71E1786C1D.quest_desc: ["Compound plate + redstone + ice canister = a &bCryo Grenade&r. Throw it: infected blocks turn to frozen biomass and infected freeze. Keep a few on you."]
	quest.3A6CCC71E1786C1D.title: "Cold Snap"
	quest.3B06108519BAEA55.quest_desc: ["Black wool, iron, a sponge. Spores and gas clouds can't get you."]
	quest.3B06108519BAEA55.title: "Breathe Easy"
	quest.3C776AC2E9F16693.quest_desc: ["Walk into the ruined city. Doors open, tables set. &7Journals say it was evacuated by rail, district by district.&r", "", "Cities are full of chests. Loot first, build later."]
	quest.3C776AC2E9F16693.title: "The Endless City"
	quest.3CADEDB868BE1BB6.quest_desc: ["At the bottom of the world the rock turns to &3sculk&r, and the sculk &chears&r: footsteps, doors, voices (proximity chat too).", "", "&eThe rules:&r sneak (&eShift&r) and you make no sound. &eWool&r blocks sound. Shriekers call &cthe Warden&r, and the Warden finds you by sound and smell. Below the Deep Dark is the &3Otherside&r, where its things live: Stalkers, Shriek Worms, Snappers, Sculk Leeches.", "", "&cTip:&r throw a snowball to make noise somewhere else. Walk into the Deep Dark to check this."]
	quest.3CADEDB868BE1BB6.quest_subtitle: "Whisper. No. Quieter than that."
	quest.3CADEDB868BE1BB6.title: "The Listening Dark"
	quest.3D4CB510549656C2.quest_desc: ["With reforged biomass and organs, the &4Mimicry&r line of weapons opens up: knife, sword, pickaxe, bow, axe, scythe... Their advancement tab shows each recipe. The strongest things in the pack."]
	quest.3D4CB510549656C2.title: "Mimicry"
	quest.3EA616D994247713.quest_desc: ["A frame of &eglowstone blocks&r, lit with a &ewater bucket&r. Islands above the sky, gentle until they are not. Don't fall."]
	quest.3EA616D994247713.title: "3. Above the Clouds"
	quest.3FC28DEE5BB9B018.quest_desc: ["The &eIron Cross&r is the one the Builders' chaplains carried: &eiron ingots&r with &elapis&r in the middle, the same shape as the wooden one. You can also upgrade a wooden cross at a smithing table.", "", "It lasts where wood breaks.", "", "&cTip:&r the Pale Demon doesn't only wear animals. If a door you closed is open, or a torch you placed is gone, hold the cross before you go in."]
	quest.3FC28DEE5BB9B018.quest_subtitle: "Heavier. Better."
	quest.3FC28DEE5BB9B018.title: "Iron Faith"
	quest.405BCA1705D5D5C2.quest_desc: ["Check this once the sun comes up. The Conductor will mark &eThe Line&r, the nearest way down into the city, on your map.", "", "The ruins on the horizon go on forever. Somebody built all of this. Somebody ran those trains. &7Where did they go?&r"]
	quest.405BCA1705D5D5C2.quest_subtitle: "Chapter Gate"
	quest.405BCA1705D5D5C2.title: "Survive the First Night"
	quest.4079353A1FC1DDC3.quest_desc: ["Compound plate, crafting table, iron sword and axe, a bottle. All infected gear is made here, from their own organs."]
	quest.4079353A1FC1DDC3.title: "The Surgery Table"
	quest.4327BAF852CCF176.quest_desc: ["Knocking at night, when everyone is home. &cNever open the door.&r Light, locks, company."]
	quest.4327BAF852CCF176.title: "The Knocker"
	quest.43D4302F02CF324C.quest_desc: ["Every patch of &3sculk&r grows out of a &3sculk catalyst&r: when something dies near one, it spreads.", "", "Dig one out (any pickaxe, &eSilk Touch&r to keep it). Up top it is a farm: kill mobs next to it and it turns their deaths into sculk instead of mess.", "", "&cTip:&r it drops XP when broken without Silk Touch. Choose.", "", "&7The Builders' note: \"IT FEEDS ON WHAT DIES NEAR IT. SO DON'T.\"&r"]
	quest.43D4302F02CF324C.quest_subtitle: "Everything down here started from one of these."
	quest.43D4302F02CF324C.title: "Where It Spreads From"
	quest.4529D0EC8EB16883.quest_desc: ["The &eZoaholic&r points you to the nearest hivemind, the brain of an outbreak."]
	quest.4529D0EC8EB16883.title: "Hivemind Radar"
	quest.461BC305191C4372.quest_desc: ["Everything the blueprint asks for. All of it is early Builder work: andesite alloy, wood and iron. Track you can pry out of any subway.", "", "Any casing works in the corners (andesite, brass, copper, train)."]
	quest.461BC305191C4372.title: "Parts List"
	quest.487EB68DB375CFD4.quest_desc: ["Mark a spot: on the big map (&eM&r) right-click and pick &eCreate Waypoint&r, or press the &e' (apostrophe)&r key where you stand.", "", "Every waypoint you make shows up on the other players' maps by itself, labelled with your name. Start a name with &e!&r to keep it private. Your friends show on your map too."]
	quest.487EB68DB375CFD4.title: "Share the Map"
	quest.4AC69566DB743EAE.quest_desc: ["Craft the &bCryo-Combat boots&r: compound plate + reinforced plate + iron boots. They clear dangerous spore foliage around you. Wear them whenever you go near infection.", "", "The rest of the set: leggings (slow nearby infected), chestplate (freeze anything close, glide), mask (spot infected in a 32x32 area). Check the advancement tab &eAnti-spore equipment&r for the recipes."]
	quest.4AC69566DB743EAE.title: "Cold Feet"
	quest.4CC4F9D09F1DDAA7.quest_desc: ["You will need people. Place a &eSupply Camp&r (craft one: press R on it) next to your base: move the preview, then confirm. Open its chest, place the &eTown Hall&r block, right-click it and name your colony. Citizens arrive.", "", "The &eYour Colony&r guide walks you through the rest."]
	quest.4CC4F9D09F1DDAA7.title: "Found a Colony"
	quest.4DCCAC87EF742EDA.quest_desc: ["A beast sleeps in the ice. Wake it only if you're ready."]
	quest.4DCCAC87EF742EDA.title: "The Frostmaw"
	quest.50BA7E2434443BCC.quest_desc: ["Hold a &elantern&r and right-click the heart while a cog is turning. Someone does the same within 15 seconds to confirm.", "", "The Engine turns for good. The dark stops coming where your lights are on. The fungus keeps coming: the Engine wants it.", "", "&7Only one of these two will ever be checked. It is one choice, for everyone on the server.&r"]
	quest.50BA7E2434443BCC.title: "Keep It Lit"
	quest.50FA11EB4D798388.quest_desc: ["Special meals dropped onto &ebiomass blocks&r give rare items and buffs, but they feed the infection. The third one (&eDesertum ultimum&r: 3 cakes, 3 dragon breath, 3 enchanted golden apples, biomass) gives the FIXER's loot. See the advancement tab."]
	quest.50FA11EB4D798388.title: "Divine Offerings"
	quest.5165942DBFBF9A95.quest_desc: ["The first time a Spore mob kills you, you won't just respawn. Take what you can from where you wake up. You leave by dying again (keepInventory is on: you keep everything), or ask an op."]
	quest.5165942DBFBF9A95.title: "If You Fall"
	quest.5188F1E9630643A3.quest_desc: ["The subways cut through older tunnels: wooden &emineshafts&r from before the city, with minecarts, rails and chests nobody came back for.", "", "Find one and walk into it. They are everywhere underground, often under a few hundred blocks of city.", "", "&cTip:&r cave spiders nest in the cobwebbed parts. Burn the webs or go around.", "", "Two stranger places are hidden down here too. Keep going."]
	quest.5188F1E9630643A3.quest_subtitle: "Wood holding up the ceiling. Hundreds of years of it."
	quest.5188F1E9630643A3.title: "Older Tunnels"
	quest.51AD8034176BFA4A.quest_desc: ["A chunk loader keeps your line running when nobody is near."]
	quest.51AD8034176BFA4A.title: "Keep Them Running"
	quest.52ED0EC9AD284615.quest_desc: ["Circuit board + compound plate + lever + observer. Scan the parts you collect to learn the creatures (Spore's own advancements track this)."]
	quest.52ED0EC9AD284615.title: "Scanning Time"
	quest.5316978AECD45C60.quest_desc: ["A flamethrower that shoots cold. Freezes whole hordes. Refuel with ice canisters: hold &eshift + right-click&r."]
	quest.5316978AECD45C60.title: "Frostwerfer"
	quest.53DD3D9328D45727.quest_desc: ["&bBlue ice&r + an iron nugget. Ammo for the cold: grenades and the Frostwerfer use it."]
	quest.53DD3D9328D45727.title: "Bottled Winter"
	quest.5511EC0E407018FF.quest_desc: ["The dark hunts where the light does not reach. Keep torches on you, and put one down wherever you stop."]
	quest.5511EC0E407018FF.title: "Light Is Life"
	quest.552775E8592A7452.quest_desc: ["Wall in your camp. A gate you can close. Light on every corner. Your builder can help, and a &eGuard Tower&r puts a guard on watch."]
	quest.552775E8592A7452.title: "Walls"
	quest.5584D611223D744A.quest_desc: ["Shafts and cogwheels carry &erotation&r. Everything in Create runs on it."]
	quest.5584D611223D744A.title: "Things That Turn"
	quest.58E40364210E9089.quest_desc: ["&cThe dangerous one.&r A &eCatalyst&r (copper, stone, an ender pearl) used on a stone-brick frame.", "", "This is where the things below came from. Go in full gear, together.", "", "&7Roots as thick as subway tunnels, all growing one way: up, toward the capital.&r"]
	quest.58E40364210E9089.title: "4. Under Everything"
	quest.599545F9AA9AB953.quest_desc: ["The giant ones: &cSieger, Gazenbreacher, Hindenburg, Howitzer, Hohlfresser&r. Break parts off them for &eReforged Biomass&r: terrestrial, aquatic and airborne kinds, one per body type. Go together."]
	quest.599545F9AA9AB953.title: "Calamity"
	quest.5A4A0B7DF4784B7E.quest_desc: ["Andesite + iron nuggets = &eandesite alloy&r, the base of nearly everything here."]
	quest.5A4A0B7DF4784B7E.title: "Builder Metal"
	quest.5A9BC6F6A674D18A.quest_desc: ["Add huts the same way: &eResidence&r (more citizens), &eForester's Hut&r (wood), &eWarehouse&r + &eCourier's Hut&r (storage and deliveries), &eGuard Tower&r (defence). Each hut's menu lets you hire and upgrade."]
	quest.5A9BC6F6A674D18A.title: "Grow the Colony"
	quest.5B2B9E2A25EC7C42.quest_desc: ["Compound plate + reinforced plate + a diamond. With &dbudding amethyst&r it upgrades every Cryo piece to &bSubZero&r (SubZero boots also clear bile)."]
	quest.5B2B9E2A25EC7C42.title: "Diamond Plate"
	quest.5C40C197C1BE9281.quest_desc: ["Those pale stalks in the sculk are &3sculk sensors&r: they light up when anything moves near them. Mine one with a &eSilk Touch&r tool and it comes with you.", "", "At home, a sensor next to a door is an alarm: hook it to a lamp or a bell with redstone, and anything walking in at night rings it.", "", "&cTip:&r wool next to a sensor blinds it."]
	quest.5C40C197C1BE9281.quest_subtitle: "If it can hear them, I can hear it."
	quest.5C40C197C1BE9281.title: "Ears in the Walls"
	quest.5FB2E35C7EFC093A.quest_desc: ["Armor fragment + fiber + mutated heart at the surgery table. Almost every infected weapon needs one."]
	quest.5FB2E35C7EFC093A.title: "A Living Core"
	quest.62B48BF4175155F9.quest_desc: ["The Builders never walked to the capital. They &eflew through the fire&r: one block in the Nether is eight up here.", "", "You need an airship first (see &eThe Builders' Craft&r). Then build a &enether portal wide enough for your ship&r (obsidian frames go up to 23x23). Your ship has to fit through the opening. The far side gets a portal the same size.", "", "Check this once it is lit."]
	quest.62B48BF4175155F9.title: "A Door Big Enough"
	quest.62D341191A8C2B01.quest_desc: ["Infected are people and animals the fungus took. &eThe rules:&r", "- Every kill they get makes them &cevolve&r into worse forms. Don't feed them: no lone fights, no dying out there.", "- They are weak to &bcold&r and starve over time.", "- It only spreads where players are. Burn it back early."]
	quest.62D341191A8C2B01.title: "First Contact"
	quest.64F936ADB8D3EDAE.quest_desc: ["Footsteps that stop when yours stop. A shape that runs on all fours, too tall to be a dog. That is &cthe Cave Dweller&r.", "", "It stalks first, then it runs. You can't really fight it. Get to light, get to people, get up a stairway.", "", "&cTip:&r if the cave sounds start getting louder, it is getting closer. Leave before they peak.", "", "Check this when you have seen it and gotten away."]
	quest.64F936ADB8D3EDAE.quest_subtitle: "I counted to ten. It didn't stop."
	quest.64F936ADB8D3EDAE.title: "The Dweller"
	quest.67EF9B6315A83728.quest_desc: ["Push the dark hard enough (kill what hunts near home, burn out a nest, light the streets) and it pushes back. Your night watch will warn you at dusk: &o\"Something's been circling the walls.\"&r", "", "That night, get everyone home. Light the edges and close the walls: they only come out of the dark. At dawn, if nothing is left near the &eTown Hall&r, you held.", "", "Managers can read the mood with &e/threat status&r."]
	quest.67EF9B6315A83728.title: "They Came For Us"
	quest.68BC051601868010.quest_desc: ["Place a station on the track. Every train is assembled here."]
	quest.68BC051601868010.title: "A Station"
	quest.6A450DB86EB3A918.quest_desc: ["A &esoul lantern&r burns blue: a torch from soul sand or soul soil inside iron nuggets.", "", "It gives less light than a lantern, but the Builders hung them in the deepest stations. The note says it keeps the ceiling dark and the floor lit, so nothing above you sees you.", "", "Craft &f4&r. You will need soul soil from the Nether later, or soul sand from a desert well if you find one."]
	quest.6A450DB86EB3A918.quest_subtitle: "Cold light. The Builders swore by it."
	quest.6A450DB86EB3A918.title: "Blue Light"
	quest.6B05E2C27F75F606.quest_desc: ["He is on the platform, by the fire. &eRight-click&r him. He never leaves it, and nothing can hurt him.", "", "Click the checkmark once you have heard him out. Right-click him again any time for the next thing to do."]
	quest.6B05E2C27F75F606.title: "Ask the Conductor"
	quest.6B3E4E3C7827C2E3.quest_desc: ["The subway engineers wore rigs with &eOcto Arms&r: pneumatic tentacles that grip walls and ceilings.", "", "A &eTentacle&r comes off a Create &esequenced assembly&r line: a &episton extension pole&r, then a &esuper glue&r (sticker) by deployer and a press, twice round. See &eThe Builders' Craft&r for presses and deployers.", "", "&cTip:&r tentacles grip &efull block faces&r only. Slabs, fences and glass panes won't hold you."]
	quest.6B3E4E3C7827C2E3.quest_subtitle: "One more hand would be nice down here."
	quest.6B3E4E3C7827C2E3.title: "A Spare Arm"
	quest.6B5362DA4D03BA83.quest_desc: ["A clipboard hangs by the cradle. Thousands of names, each with a time.", "&o\"Everyone takes a shift. Everyone. Hands on the cranks until the relief train comes.\"&r", "", "The last hundred rows are one name, in one hand, getting shakier. &7No relief train came.&r"]
	quest.6B5362DA4D03BA83.title: "The Shift Roster"
	quest.6BA10BBEC0AC73D5.quest_desc: ["Every stairway in the city goes down to the old subway.", "", "The tunnels are how the Builders moved everyone, and the fastest way across the city if you know them. Carry &f16&r &etorches&r before you go down; that is the price of the ticket. Bring a friend.", "", "Listen: every so often a &eghost train&r passes. A far whistle, the lamps flicker, nobody driving. The lit stations are the only places the dark will not follow.", "", "&7Every station map agrees on one thing: all the lines run off the edge of the map.&r"]
	quest.6BA10BBEC0AC73D5.quest_subtitle: "Every stairway down smells like wet iron."
	quest.6BA10BBEC0AC73D5.title: "Into the Tunnels"
	quest.6BFB5539D1CEC86A.quest_desc: ["You wake on a cold platform. The train that brought you is already pulling away, &oon schedule&r, with no driver. (The platform is still there, beside your camp.)", "", "This book is your journal. &eThe Line&r is the story: where to go next. The &eField Guides&r teach the mods. Do those in any order.", "", "Click the checkmark to begin. The man in the cap on the platform is the &eConductor&r."]
	quest.6BFB5539D1CEC86A.title: "Last Stop"
	quest.6C534E757D9A0FE8.quest_desc: ["Propellers + a frame + Create Aeronautics = an &eairship&r. The Line's last act needs one."]
	quest.6C534E757D9A0FE8.title: "Lift"
	quest.6CBC9732078BA896.quest_desc: ["From the air the Nether is a map: lava seas, fortress walls, and the old Builder roads running straight toward where the capital stands above.", "", "Find a &efortress&r without touching the ground. Ghasts will see you coming."]
	quest.6CBC9732078BA896.title: "Over the Lava Sea"
	quest.6E36006FC0490D84.quest_desc: ["Check this when your train moves."]
	quest.6E36006FC0490D84.title: "Your Own Train"
	quest.6EAAA80B8271EADD.quest_desc: ["The &eC.D.U.&r freezes everything around it. The infection hates cold: put one at the edge of your colony."]
	quest.6EAAA80B8271EADD.title: "Local Ice Age"
	quest.70A326F4FA46F353.quest_desc: ["In the engineer's booth, a logbook open on the desk:", "&o\"The Engine does not make light from nothing. It burns what grows under the capital. The fungus is the fuel. As long as it turns it pulls the growth up and burns it, and the light keeps the dark below.", "", "When we ran short of hands it slowed, and the fuel got out. You know the rest.", "", "Whoever reads this: you can keep it turning, and it will want feeding forever. Or you can stop it for good. The growth will sink back where it came from, and nothing will hold the dark. I could not choose.", "", "A lantern on the heart to keep it lit. A wrench to let it rest.\"&r"]
	quest.70A326F4FA46F353.title: "The Last Entry"
	quest.7212199C40E6A57E.quest_desc: ["An arrivals board under the capital, still lit:", "&o\"ARRIVALS TODAY: 212. DEPARTURES: 0.\"&r", "", "A booth full of tickets. Every one says the same thing: &o\"ONE WAY. ENGINE WORKS.\"&r", "", "The evacuation trains were never leaving. They were coming &ehere&r."]
	quest.7212199C40E6A57E.title: "Platform Zero"
	quest.724A72FEF87C257E.quest_desc: ["Walk to the &earrival platform&r beside your camp: a few rails, a station block, a departures board under a lit lamp. Read the board. Every train is &oon time&r. None will ever come.", "", "The trains still run, with no one to drive them. Listen for them near track, and underground. Check this once you have read the board."]
	quest.724A72FEF87C257E.title: "Catch the Line"
	quest.733C295A6FE4F1AA.quest_desc: ["Fly the airship into the portal. Ship, crew, seats and cargo all go through together. &cMobs and dropped items stay behind.&r", "", "Each trip costs about a tenth of your speed. The far side is cleared so you don't land in basalt.", "", "&7Back up the world before your first crossing: airship physics can break.&r"]
	quest.733C295A6FE4F1AA.title: "Through the Fire"
	quest.74B4C215DE2037A9.quest_desc: ["Not everything down here is an animal. Some of it &cwears&r them: a cow that stands too still, a villager that smiles too long. The Builders called it &cthe Pale Demon&r.", "", "They fought it with crosses. The cheapest is &f5&r &esticks&r: three across the top, two down the middle.", "", "&cTip:&r it is a start, not armor. Hold it, don't trust it.", "", "Next: a better one, with something that sparks."]
	quest.74B4C215DE2037A9.quest_subtitle: "I don't believe in anything. I made one anyway."
	quest.74B4C215DE2037A9.title: "Two Sticks and a Prayer"
	quest.76016D8C7E4E16A2.quest_desc: ["A mixer over a basin. Heated with a blaze burner later, it makes &ebrass&r."]
	quest.76016D8C7E4E16A2.title: "Mixing"
	quest.78075ECAC362C9CB.quest_desc: ["The deepest tunnels end in &3sculk&r: black-blue growth that &chears&r. Footsteps, doors, voices. Proximity chat counts.", "", "&eWool&r blocks sound. Carry &f8&r &ewhite wool&r and lay it over any path you will walk twice. Sneaking (&eShift&r) makes no sound at all.", "", "&cTip:&r a thrown snowball or arrow makes noise where it lands. Use that to pull things away from you.", "", "Next: go down to where the sculk starts."]
	quest.78075ECAC362C9CB.quest_subtitle: "Whisper. No. Quieter than that."
	quest.78075ECAC362C9CB.title: "Soft Steps"
	quest.7812CC40D6BF64EE.quest_desc: ["Some shafts were sealed from the &einside&r. Planks nailed over the openings, crosses on the floor, unlit torches still in their holders.", "", "Find an &eAbandoned Shaft&r. The miners who worked it left in a hurry and left their things behind.", "", "&cTip:&r if the torches are out when you arrive, something put them out. Re-light them before you go further in."]
	quest.7812CC40D6BF64EE.quest_subtitle: "Who nails the planks on from the inside?"
	quest.7812CC40D6BF64EE.title: "Abandoned Shafts"
	quest.78EED41DDBE9C532.quest_desc: ["Fly back out through a portal with the ship in one piece.", "", "&eShortcut:&r eight blocks of the Nether is a long way over the city. Build a second big portal at the far end of a Nether flight and you can cross the overworld in minutes."]
	quest.78EED41DDBE9C532.title: "Bring Her Home"
	quest.7A7A2ABF199241D6.quest_desc: ["&eEasiest first.&r Dig a 2x2 pool of water, ring it with flowers, throw in a &ediamond&r.", "", "It is always dusk there. Follow the Magic Map to the bosses in order. Some Builders hid here."]
	quest.7A7A2ABF199241D6.title: "1. The Forest at Dusk"
	quest.7B91185463CC20A0.quest_desc: ["Build it where the rail stops. Get a cog turning, then right-click the heart with an &eempty hand&r. If anything is missing, it will tell you what.", "", "&cBefore you do:&r everyone geared, everyone there. Whatever lives under the capital has been listening for that sound for a hundred years."]
	quest.7B91185463CC20A0.title: "Seat the Heart"
	quest.7C354DBEC8EEE180.quest_desc: ["The Conductor read you the list; &e/keys&r prints it again. The two that matter now: hold &e`&r (left of 1) while mining to take the whole vein, and &eM&r for the map. &eCaps Lock&r is proximity voice: the things out there hear it too."]
	quest.7C354DBEC8EEE180.title: "Your Keys"
	quest.7D0BC39519E50BC5.quest_desc: ["You have a home, people, and light.", "", "Next: &eBelow the Line&r. If you want trains and machines, start &eThe Builders' Craft&r now. It runs alongside the story; the story never waits on it."]
	quest.7D0BC39519E50BC5.quest_subtitle: "Chapter Gate"
	quest.7D0BC39519E50BC5.title: "District One Is Lit"
	quest.7E00ED1B6FF5E185.quest_desc: ["The chests of the Ancient City hold &3echo shards&r: crystals that remember sound.", "", "Collect &f4&r. Quietly: the city is full of sensors and shriekers. Crouch everywhere, and open chests from the side.", "", "&cTip:&r the city's soul fire gives off light, but it is not safe light. Things still spawn on the sculk floor.", "", "Next: an echo shard can find the place you last died."]
	quest.7E00ED1B6FF5E185.quest_subtitle: "Hold one to your ear. Don't."
	quest.7E00ED1B6FF5E185.title: "Echoes"
	quest.7EC4EE217864875C.quest_desc: ["It stops. The cogs tick down, the heart goes dark, and for the first time in a hundred years nothing under the capital is being pulled.", "", "The fungus lets go. Fewer infected every night, and none near the Engine.", "", "But the light was only ever borrowed. The faces don't leave at dawn any more, and on dark nights the dark comes closer. You chose a world with no fuel in it. &cLearn to live in it.&r", "", "&7The End of the Line.&r"]
	quest.7EC4EE217864875C.title: "Lights Out"
	quest.7F38C96463632CCB.quest_desc: ["&cThe Silencing Golem&r hides in plain sight: it looks like the cave wall until you are next to it.", "", "&eThe rules:&r it lives in quiet tunnels and caves. It waits, then it moves. It can be killed.", "", "Watch walls that sit slightly wrong, and blocks that weren't there on the way in. Fight it in the light with a friend.", "", "&cTip:&r carry cobblestone to wall it off and buy time."]
	quest.7F38C96463632CCB.quest_subtitle: "That wall wasn't there on the way in."
	quest.7F38C96463632CCB.title: "The Silencing Golem"
	quest.7F67B3AD904BA91C.quest_desc: ["Before any other world: &eiron armor or better&r, a stack of food, a bed at home, torches, and a friend. You can always come back.", "", "Go in this order. Each one is harder than the last."]
	quest.7F67B3AD904BA91C.title: "Ready Check"
	quest.7FD40EEA4B925728.quest_desc: ["Amethyst dust + sugar = &eCompound&r. Smelt it into a &eCompound Plate&r, the Builders' anti-infection material."]
	quest.7FD40EEA4B925728.title: "Compound Plate"
	quest.7FF8B824E03C98EF.quest_desc: ["Torches burn out of your hands fast down here. Lanterns hang from the ceiling, out of reach of whatever walks the platforms.", "", "Craft &f4&r &elanterns&r (a torch inside iron nuggets) and hang one at every stairway you use. A lit stairway is a way home.", "", "&cTip:&r light the &etop&r of a stairway too, not just the bottom. Things wait where the light stops.", "", "&7A Builder note on a lamp post: \"IF IT GOES OUT, YOU GO UP.\"&r"]
	quest.7FF8B824E03C98EF.quest_subtitle: "Something to see by that isn't on fire in my hand."
	quest.7FF8B824E03C98EF.title: "A Lamp That Stays"
